# Sample .wslconfig for running the local kind cluster on Windows/WSL2.
#
# WHY: the default WSL2 VM on the build machine had only ~1.9 GB RAM, which is not enough to run a
# kind Kubernetes control-plane plus the platform workloads — the VM OOM-crashed under load.
#
# IMPORTANT — size this to YOUR host, not blindly:
#   WSL2 shares the host's physical RAM with Windows. Only give WSL2 ~50-75% of TOTAL host RAM and
#   always leave ~2-3 GB for Windows itself. Setting `memory` higher than the host has, or so high
#   that Windows is starved, will make the WHOLE machine swap/hang.
#
#   * Host >= 16 GB : memory=8GB  processors=4   (comfortable for kind + this stack)
#   * Host == 8 GB  : memory=5GB  processors=4   (tight; run the `dev` overlay, not `ha`)
#   * Host <= 4 GB  : a local Kubernetes cluster is NOT recommended — even an idle kind
#                     control-plane (~2 GB) plus Windows (~2 GB) exceeds the host. Prefer running
#                     the app directly (backend + worker + frontend via `npm`/`vite`) instead of on
#                     kind, or use a machine/VM with more RAM for the k8s deployment steps.
#
# INSTALL:
#   1. Copy this file to  C:\Users\<your-user>\.wslconfig  (edit `memory` for your host per above)
#   2. From PowerShell:   wsl --shutdown
#   3. Re-open WSL and bring the cluster up again (see scripts/ and README).

[wsl2]
# Example for a 16 GB host. LOWER this if your host has less RAM (see guidance above).
memory=8GB
processors=4
swap=2GB
